{"title":"The Hummingbird Bike","link":"https://kottke.org/25/09/the-hummingbird-bike","date":1758816181000,"content":"\n        <p><img src=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/hummingbird-bike.jpg\" srcset=\"/cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=500,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/hummingbird-bike.jpg 500w, /cdn-cgi/image/format=auto,fit=scale-down,width=1200,metadata=none/plus/misc/images/hummingbird-bike.jpg 1200w\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1300\" height=\"732\" alt=\"a very sleek bike called the Hummingbird bike\" /></p>\n\n<p>Gooood lord, just look at <a href=\"https://tomato.co.uk/journal/hummingbird\">this exquisite handmade bike</a>, a collaboration between British design collective Tomato<sup><a href=\"#fn:1758810826\">1</a></sup> and Shinichi Konno of <a href=\"http://www.cherubim.jp/\">Cherubim</a>.</p>\n\n<ol><p><li>Karl Hyde and Rick Smith of the electronic group Underworld are Tomato co-founders. I found my way to this bike after watching <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rAOHJqJMYDA\">Underworld’s recent Boiler Room set</a>.’<a href=\"#fnref:1758810826\">↩</a></li></p></ol>\n\n        \n\n         <p><strong>Tags:</strong> <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/bicycles\">bicycles</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/biking\">biking</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/design\">design</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/Shinichi%20Konno\">Shinichi Konno</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/Tomato\">Tomato</a> · <a href=\"https://kottke.org/tag/Underworld\">Underworld</a></p>\n\n         <p>💬 <a href=\"https://kottke.org/25/09/the-hummingbird-bike\">Join the discussion on kottke.org</a> →</p>\n\n    ","author":"Jason Kottke","siteTitle":"Kottke","siteHash":"89a883271b4598f9b33ebe87be70d38557bcd266e68aee521a8f93622e0ab723","entryHash":"7fbc0427dc7e72cb029c799f2a0c39f800e63114b66733e5e135c4d0ed3d65e8","category":"Sites"}